		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4183&amp;p=35643#p35643"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>This is awesome! I started a fork to to support North America and went down a rabbit hole with it.<br><br>Changes:<ul><li> Supports North America and Rest of World (In Theory)</li><li> Added the ability to choose states. Just choosing United States has a max limit and may not include your locations.</li><li> Limits Channel import to 80 channels, which is the max per zone</li><li> Changed the PL/TSQL and Squelch to match the official OpenGD77 output from Repeaterbook.</li><li> Supports points and commas in output</li><li> Added delay in US calls to not hit the endpoint more than 2 times a minute.</li><li> Added some print statements so you can see the progress. Doing 2 or more states takes a few minutes to complete.</li></ul>You can find it here: <a href="https://github.com/desertblade/OpenGD77-Repeaterbook" class="postlink">https://github.com/desertblade/OpenGD77-Repeaterbook</a></div></blockquote>Thank you for updating this on 6 Feb 25 with regards to a Repeaterbook change in the API!<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5571">N0JYZ</a> — Fri Feb 07, 2025 2:37 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
